---
title: Sheetpan Sausage Sweet Potato Gnocchi
description: Cozy sheetpan dinner of sausage, sweet potato, red onion, and gnocchi roasted until browned, finished with goat cheese and hot honey.
course: Main
source: 🧠
image: https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRPoHZmaOYw6qekJmvIzV3jumtfUoa1HxlV1I-yETHPPw&s=10
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 35 minutes
servings: 4
---

Preheat the #oven{} to 425F.

On a #sheet pan{}, toss @sausage{1%lb}(spicy Italian is great, or whatever your family likes), @red onion{1}(chopped), @gnocchi{1%pack}, and @sweet potato{1}(cubed) with @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @garlic salt{1%tsp}, and @dried thyme{1%tsp}(or rosemary or any dried herb). Spread into an even layer.

Bake for ~{25-35%minutes}, stirring once halfway through, until browned and the sweet potato is tender.

Finish with @goat cheese{}(crumbled) and a drizzle of @hot honey{}(or regular honey).
